<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amlapura</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amlapura is a town in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, and the capital of Karangasem Regency. It was the seat of the rajas of Karangasem, who in the 18th century also ruled western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombok">Lombok</a>, and the last kings built its palace, the Puri Agung Karangasem, and the nearby water palaces of Ujung and Tirta Gangga. The town, formerly called Karangasem, took the name Amlapura after the eruption of Mount Agung in 1963.</p></div>
